+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0196piBKACXfidTayxWj93zP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T14: Financial Ledger\n2\t\n3\t**Category:** bugfix/hard\n4\t**Timeout:** 30 minutes\n5\t\n6\t## Description\n7\t\n8\tYou're maintaining a double-entry accounting ledger library. The library tracks accounts, journal entries (transactions), and provides reporting functions (trial balance, account statements, P&L).\n9\t\n10\tSeveral bugs have been reported. The test suite has 40 tests, but only 31 are currently passing (8 bugs cause 9 test failures). Your job is to fix all the bugs so that all 40 tests pass.\n11\t\n12\t## Architecture\n13\t\n14\tThe library is in `src/ledger.ts` and exports:\n15\t\n16\t- `Ledger` class with methods:\n17\t  - `createAccount(name, type, currency?)` — Create a named account (asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense). Optional currency defaults to \"USD\".\n18\t  - `postEntry(description, debits, credits, date?)` — Post a journal entry with debit/credit line items. Each line is `{ account: string, amount: number }`. Debits must equal credits. Optional date defaults to now.\n19\t  - `getBalance(accountName)` — Get current balance for an account. Assets/expenses have normal debit balances; liabilities/equity/revenue have normal credit balances.\n20\t  - `getTrialBalance()` — Returns all account balances. Total debits must equal total credits.\n21\t  - `getStatement(accountName, startDate?, endDate?)` — Returns chronological list of entries affecting an account, with running balance.\n22\t  - `splitEntry(description, fromAccount, toAccounts, totalAmount, date?)` — Convenience method: split a total amount across multiple destination accounts. `toAccounts` is `{ account: string, amount: number }[]`. Creates a journal entry debiting `fromAccount` and crediting each destination.\n23\t  - `getAccountsByType(type)` — Returns all accounts of a given type.\n24\t  - `getProfitAndLoss(startDate?, endDate?)` — Returns revenue minus expenses for the period.\n25\t\n26\t## Known Issues\n27\t\n28\tUsers have reported:\n29\t1. Trial balance doesn't balance in some scenarios\n30\t2. Account statements show wrong running balances\n31\t3. Split entries sometimes create unbalanced journal entries\n32\t4. Date filtering in statements is off-by-one\n33\t5. P&L calculation has sign errors\n34\t6. Currency mismatch validation isn't working\n35\t7. Duplicate account names aren't rejected\n36\t8. getBalance returns wrong sign for liability accounts\n37\t\n38\t## Validation\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\tnpm test      # Run tests (32/40 passing currently)\n42\tnpm run build # Should compile cleanly\n43\tnpm run lint  # Should pass\n44\t```\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LybfWFL8t6zZTxsicypQ4i","session_id":"25cb8311-97ae-472b-bc2e-2933f28ff522","uuid":"b9bae03e-ad4c-49bd-bf51-c5662cbd8979","timestamp":"2026-07-25T02:04:47.682Z","subagent_type":"conclave:code-reviewer","task_description":"Review ledger bugfix"}
